[2026-09-20 12:35:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 050]   The sharpest TEP prediction in the ideas file: if the solar system's
[2026-09-20 12:35:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 050]   anomalous directions are all projections of a single proper-time
[2026-09-20 12:35:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 050]   field structure, they should not merely "roughly align" -- they
[2026-09-20 12:35:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 050]   should be the same map.  This step collects the measured TNO
[2026-09-20 12:35:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 050]   clustering axis from step_02 plus every independently published
[2026-09-20 12:35:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 050]   anomalous direction, converts all of them to J2000 ecliptic
[2026-09-20 12:35:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 050]   coordinates, and runs a spherical concentration test.
[2026-09-20 12:35:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 050]   Axes included (all real, published values; sources listed):
